  "docs.d0215": "Generation timed out",
  "docs.d0216": "Two generation methods",
  "docs.d0217": "The platform selects the generation method based on model in the request:\n\n1. model is a published image model (e.g. codex-image, listed in GET /v1/models): the model generates images directly and accepts only a prompt. n must be 1; response_format must be b64_json. size, quality, and background accept only auto (equivalent to omission). style, output_format, output_compression, moderation, partial_images, and stream (when true) all return 400 unsupported_parameter. revised_prompt in the response is the prompt actually used by the model.\n\n2. model is omitted or is not an image model: uses the platform's preset image workflow. prompt is bound to the workflow. size/quality/style are available only if supported by the workflow; otherwise they return 400 unsupported_parameter. response_format=url is supported. Other OpenAI fields, such as background and output_format, are ignored in this mode. If no image workflow is configured, returns 404 endpoint_not_configured.\n\nIf you specify an image model ID with no available instances, the request uses method 2; it is not silently switched to another image model.",
